      "updated_at": "2017-05-01T23:57:55Z",
      "body": "Yas! First pass notes summing up the conversation so far and my thoughts and questions.\r\n\r\nPRIMARY: Patients who are 120 days + past the [DATE] should be archived\r\n\r\n  -  Needs:\r\n     - patient privacy - remove no longer needed PII \r\n     - system limitation - phone number based ID conflicts\r\n     - process is irreversible\r\n  -  Wants\r\n     - same patients archive linked somehow? (is this a need?)\r\n     - use a concern `patient_archiving_concern`\r\n     - invoke via `@patient.archive!`\r\n  - Approach\r\n     - Archive flag: on\r\n     - Convert PII to non-PII for reporting needs\r\n     - Shred PII data (any _non whitelisted_ data)\r\n     - make patient read only?\r\n  - PII Conversion\r\n     -  Other Contact has data? -> set a flag\r\n     - appt date changed? after pledge sent? -> set a flag\r\n     - clinic changed?  after pledge sent? -> set a flag\r\n     - other?\r\n  - Outstanding Questions\r\n     - 120 days past what? Initial Call? Appt Date? LMP?\r\n     - how does the archive method get called? Button? Cron?\r\n     - what does this do to views?\r\n     - does this break patient field validations?\r\n     - how to handle logs?\r\n        - Kat leaning towards nuking them completely ",
      "author_association": "MEMBER",
      "pin": null,
