      "created_at": "2017-05-05T23:08:08Z",
      "updated_at": "2017-05-05T23:08:08Z",
      "body": "re: same patients linked somehow, I think the ideal here is that the same patients will share IDs, and we'll be able to group them by that. We can use `patient_identifier` for that, which we can generate by some scramble or some consistent business logic. This is a DCAF need (DCAF is interested in what repeat users of our service look like).\r\n\r\nPatient read only would be great. I think if after archiving it requires rooting around in the rails console, that's a great outcome.\r\n\r\n120 days should probably be after a pledge is sent. But we might want to crank that up. Let's set it at 120 past pledge until we come up a better plan though.\r\n\r\nre: calling archive method, There's a nightly cleanup rake task that gets called which we can hook into; we can probably define this as a class method on Patient and call it from there. \r\n\r\nre: views, In a nutshell, they should stop being searchable.\r\n\r\nre: validations, it'll blow up a lot of them, but rails will let us work around this use case by setting validations. See the current validation on the pregnancy model, for example, which fires certain validations IF an attribute is true -- we can do something similar for patient, enforcing phone/name if archived is false. \r\n\r\n+1 on nuking audit logs. ",
      "author_association": "MEMBER",
      "pin": null,
