      "updated_at": "2017-05-11T00:36:53Z",
      "body": "re:re: same patient linked somehow, I've been mulling on this. We are using public info (phone number) plus public (open source) business logic. If a person knew someone's phone number they could apply the archive ID-scramble process and know the new ID and effectively remove the anonymity. (See [De-anonymization](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/De-anonymization))\r\n\r\nSo, which we need is some secret salt, probably stored as an ENV? Are there best practices for salted hashing in ruby that you prefer @colinxfleming? I'll start researching.",
      "author_association": "MEMBER",
      "pin": null,
