      "created_at": "2017-05-20T05:14:42Z",
      "updated_at": "2017-05-20T05:16:52Z",
      "body": "The yellows, with my comments, are:\r\n\r\n* **age (rounding/range appropriate?)** Yes, moving to a range would be perfect.\r\n* **Spanish?** This does tend to have an impact on program delivery, I'd favor keeping it.\r\n* **City** Probably no need unless we want to look at questions like 'how far do our patients tend to travel'. I could go either way on this.\r\n* **County** We don't use this, it's more for Baltimore. I suspect they'll want to keep it for business reasons I won't get into here.\r\n* **Relationship** Nuke it\r\n* **Adults in household** We only really need this to gauge NAF eligibility. Nuke it.\r\n* **Minors in household** Same deal, definitely nuke it.\r\n* **Circumstances** I'm REASONABLY sure we can ditch this. I don't see any particular reason why we should keep it unless there's a data question.\r\n\r\n@alisonnjones should get final say on these.\r\n",
      "author_association": "MEMBER",
