      "body": "@alisonnjones we had thought a bit about \"incomplete\" status patients, but hadn't gotten any user-buy in yet, so that's awesome to get! :100: \r\n\r\nI like the two-catch archive idea.  \r\nPatients archiving after fulfillment (maybe delayed ~7 days in case of corrections? accountant input needed there) is a great first trigger for scramble.   \r\nThen we just need to consider the outside bound for scrambling un-fulfilled patients. What's the longest reasonable timeline for a clinic to contact us re:fulfillment? We probably want to double that to avoid being unable to fulfill delayed clinics?",
